   home to any external server.

5. WINDOWS REGISTRY & FILE ASSOCIATION NOTICE
   If you enable Windows Context Menu or "Open with..." integration during
   setup, the installer writes per-user file association entries under
   `HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Classes` and `HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\RiverLook`.
   These entries can be cleanly removed at any time using the uninstaller,
   via Windows "Installed Apps", or via the in-app "Options ->
   Unregister Windows Associations" command.

